# Keep the build context small. The image only needs:
#   requirements_optimized.txt, entrypoint*.sh, controller/, agent/, config/, shared/
# Everything below is excluded — without this the context is ~1.24 GB (mostly
# saved image tarballs and local test results) to ship a ~1 MB application, and
# every build pays that cost.
#
# NOTE: this is an exclude-list, not an allow-list, so a new source directory
# still ships by default. Only add entries you are sure the Dockerfile's COPY
# lines do not need.

# ── Saved container images (~850 MB) ─────────────────────────────
*.tar

# ── Local development data: SQLite db, synced scripts, run results ──
local_data/

# ── Version control and editor state ─────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# ── Docs toolchain (node_modules alone is most of it) ────────────
docs/

# ── Not used by the runtime image ────────────────────────────────
k8s/
alpha-automation-scripts/
scripts/
README.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
run_local.ps1
run_and_push.sh
requirements.txt
"requirements_optimized - Copy.txt"

# ── Python / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
